{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"No. Indigenous peoples have faced extensive racial persecution, including forced displacement, massacres, suppression of languages and cultural practices, and policies aimed at forcibly assimilating them.\n\nExamples include the forced removal of Native American nations in the United States, residential schools in Canada, and the removal of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander children from their families in Australia—the Stolen Generations.\n\nExperiences vary across peoples, places, and periods, but the claim that Indigenous people have **never** faced racial persecution is historically false."}}
